# =============================================================================
# .gitignore -- repo ROOT. The paths below are relative to THIS directory, which
# is the parent of "Converted Minecraft in rust/".
#
# # A PATTERN CONTAINING A SEPARATOR IS ANCHORED TO THE .gitignore's OWN DIRECTORY.
#
# That rule is the whole reason session 07's cleanup silently did nothing. The first
# version of this file carried
#
#     _porting/java-oracle/lib/
#
# which looks right and matches nothing, because the real path is
#
#     Converted Minecraft in rust/_porting/java-oracle/lib/
#
# `git rm --cached` staged the deletions, then `git add -A` saw a path that no
# ignore rule covered and put the 29 jars straight back. Session 07's report claimed
# they were untracked. They were not. Session 08's reviewer found them on GitHub.
#
# So: patterns with a separator get the `Converted Minecraft in rust/` prefix, and
# every claim about git state is proved with `git check-ignore` and `git ls-files`
# output in the session report rather than asserted.
# =============================================================================

# Build output. `target/` is large, machine-specific, and fully reproducible from
# Cargo.lock; committing it makes every diff meaningless.
target/
**/target/

# Python bytecode. `_porting/tools/*.py` are READ-ONLY reporters (see the rule in
# SESSION_LOG.md) but they still get run, and CPython writes these next to them.
# No separator, so these match at ANY depth.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Compiled oracle classes. Rebuilt by every `run.ps1` invocation.
*.class

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The oracle's downloaded dependencies and its logs.
#
# `_porting/java-oracle/lib/*.jar` are THIRD-PARTY BINARIES, several of them tens of
# megabytes, and one of them (`authlib`) is a PROPRIETARY Mojang library. None of it
# belongs in this repository. Re-fetch with:
#
#     powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass \
#         -File "Converted Minecraft in rust/_porting/java-oracle/fetch_libs.ps1"
#
# `authlib` in particular must never be committed: it is not ours to redistribute.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Converted Minecraft in rust/_porting/java-oracle/lib/
Converted Minecraft in rust/_porting/java-oracle/logs/

# The crate-root `logs/` too. The oracle writes to BOTH
# `_porting/java-oracle/logs/` and `Converted Minecraft in rust/logs/`, and session 07
# only covered the first -- which is how one `latest.log` survived while the other did
# not, and neither was noticed until the reviewer diffed the tree.
Converted Minecraft in rust/logs/

# Editor / OS noise. No separators except the trailing `/`, so these match at any depth.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini